A recent priest of mine developed a rare skill of eating/fighting while
unconscious, alias he didn't live very long to make use of his new
talent.

On reaching level 3, Agayn the pious found himself to be weak and
without victuals. He called on Crom, the almighty, to relieve his
plight. Alas, this was not to be - "Thou art arrogant, mortal! Goodbye
level 4." boomed the diety. Sigh.

Agayn engaged in several fights to procure the nutrition he required,
in vain, for all the monsters he killed left no corpses (a rare and
strange party trick). Soon he began fainting with hunger, whereupon he
found a tin. He consumed the soup therein, but was still "fainting".
Thereafter he consumed a hobbit corpse and lo! While "fainted" he was
able to fight and kill an orc. While eating that, he was stopped by
an acidic protoplasm.  After killing the acid blob that had
interrupted his meal he continued and I got the message:

	"Your resume your meal. You regain consciousness."

How was I able to fight an orc and eat it, while out cold??


Jan.

Eh, Agayn? Oh, he died a few turns later at the hands of a mighty
killer newt.


